      "lf": 2,
      "text": "name: es-rental-income"
    },
    {
      "lf": 3,
      "text": "description: Use this Guide to compute common-territory Spanish individual rental and own-use property income for 2026. It covers ownership and income classification, gross rent, property-specific interest and repair caps, other expenses, bad debts, depreciation and lifetime limits, residential net-income reductions, the October reform and December lease-date transition, relative lettings and imputed income. Trigger phrases include alquiler Espa\u00f1a, arrendamiento vivienda, rendimiento capital inmobiliario, reducci\u00f3n alquiler, amortizaci\u00f3n inmueble, gastos reparaci\u00f3n, renta imputada and landlord tax Spain. Obtain actual lease and renewal dates, tenant use and age, prior rent and reference-price evidence, large-holder status, cadastral values, acquisition costs, rental days and prior expense ledgers. Resident rental results feed the full state and regional IRPF computation. Non-resident income, property businesses, corporate landlords and indirect-tax treatment have separate companion routes."
    },
